      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "pse:cc-327-2026-05-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "pse:cc-327-2026-05-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 5 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Sheet 327-A prices the Basic Charge at \"$7.49 single phase or $17.99 three phase\". Only the single-phase $7.49 is carried, as a Price with no condition, so it applies to every customer and a three-phase customer's monthly charge is $10.50 low. (2) Schedule 81 (Tax Adjustment) increases \"the rates and charges named in this tariff\" by the effect of a municipal tax that varies by jurisdiction, from 2.136 percent to 9.119 percent in the Sheet 81 tables. Not carried; the Summary Sheet also excludes it (\"Rates in this summary include the effect of all supplemental rate schedules except Schedule 81\"). A bill inside a taxing jurisdiction resolves low by that percentage of every charge. (3) Sheet 327-B BILL PROTECTION: an annual bill credit, for low-income Customers selected for bill protection in the pilot that ended September 30, 2025, of Energy Charge costs more than 10 percent above what Schedule 7 would have charged. Not carried. It reaches only those pilot participants, and its value is a bill recomputed under Schedule 7, which no Price here can state. (4) Exemptions in the supplemental schedules are not carried: neither Schedule 111 rate applies to a Customer taking optional Schedule 139 service or registered as a National Security Entity, and Schedule 141A does not apply to a Customer who took Schedule 139 service on or before that schedule's original effective date. Both rates are carried as Prices with no condition, so such a customer resolves $0.009637 per kWh low on Schedule 111 (whose net rate is a credit) and $0.002010 per kWh high on Schedule 141A. (5) Native American Heritage Day is carried as dated urpx:Holiday entries for each year from this version's year through 2040. Sheet 327-B defines it as \"The Friday immediately following the fourth Thursday in November\", which a rule of the form \"Fourth Friday in November\" gets wrong in years when November 1 is a Friday, so no rule string is carried. Each year after 2040 needs a further dated entry.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-05T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
